          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Walking backwards on a treadmill</strong> works the quads and
            calves harder, is gentler on the front of the knee for many people, challenges balance
            and burns more energy at the same speed. It is a legitimate tool, used in some
            rehabilitation settings, rather than a gimmick.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
